From 5604212da9285d92729a0028e9bb51bb0ebbba30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:41:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hand a pairing file opened from another app to Cartouche's
 setup

The player's Mac exports the pairing file with iloader and sends it to
the iPhone, by AirDrop or through iCloud Drive. LiveContainer opens any
file it is given as an app to install. A file with a pairing file's
extension (.plist, .mobiledevicepairing or .mobiledevicepair) now goes
to Cartouche's setup instead, which checks it and puts it where the
built-in SideStore reads it, then the app shows its games; any other
file still goes to the Apps tab. The setup in launcher/Sources does the
work, so that a large IPA is never read here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJorvBGmBB88WUcRVhE7
---
 LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift b/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift
index f78102c..6df405c 100644
--- a/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift
+++ b/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift
@@ -119,6 +119,12 @@ struct LCTabView: View {
     func dispatchURL(url: URL) {
         repeat {
             if url.isFileURL {
+                // Cartouche: a pairing file opened from AirDrop or Files goes
+                // to Cartouche's setup, not to the app installer.
+                if CartouchePairing.openedFile(url) {
+                    sharedModel.selectedTab = .initial
+                    return
+                }
                 sharedModel.selectedTab = .apps
                 break
             }
